<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?>
<!--
    The pasture adapter (RLPastureSeason, RLMeadowSeason): the fresh grass of a pen's own pasture
    (husbandry meadow) through the winter. A copy in the mod's modSettings folder replaces this
    file. Wool shearing seasons are in breedTraits.xml (woolShearing).

    There is one DEFAULT preset and any number of map presets. A map preset applies when
    one of its `maps` (mod names, space separated) is the loaded map; else DEFAULT does.

    Only pens with a pasture (sheep, cattle, horses: any husbandry meadow). Normal fields, mown
    grass and anything in a trough (grass, hay, silage) are never touched.

    The edible share of the pasture's fresh grass follows the season, in model days (a game month
    is 30 model days at any days-per-month setting):

      ramp down   from the first dormant month on, rampDownDays to fall from 1 to dormantFactor;
                  the grass the factor takes away is gone (it withered), and a growth update in
                  this time adds nothing back
      dormant     the rest of the dormant months: dormantFactor; a growth update or a month change
                  restores nothing
      recovery    from the first growing month on: what the map's growth gives, less the share
                  of the pasture's grass area not grown back yet (1 - factor, the factor rising
                  from dormantFactor to 1 over rampUpDays); nothing comes back that withered in
                  the autumn
      warning     warnDays before the ramp down starts, the pen's owner is told to provide
                  supplementary feed (hay or silage in the trough)

    The pen's food rows, the info box, the ration planner and what the animals eat all see the
    same edible amount.

    dormancy      AUTO: dormant months are those in which the map's growth table (foliage
                  growth.seasonal) lets none of the pasture's fruit types grow into or within its
                  eatable states (Hof Bergmann's grass and meadow: late autumn, early and mid
                  winter). PERIODS: the months in dormantPeriods (EARLY_SPRING .. LATE_WINTER).
    enabled       false: the pasture behaves as the base game's.
    With seasonal growth off (growth mode daily or disabled) the factor is 1 all year.

    The 14 days and the factor 0 are a game fit for Hof Bergmann's winters, not an ecological rule:
    mild climates graze through the winter (AHDB deferred grazing), which a map's own growth table
    expresses by growing in those months, and then AUTO finds no dormancy.
-->
<pastureSeasons>
    <meadow>
        <preset name="DEFAULT" enabled="true" dormancy="AUTO" rampDownDays="14" rampUpDays="14" dormantFactor="0" warnDays="7"/>
        <preset name="HOF_BERGMANN" maps="FS25_HofBergmann" enabled="true" dormancy="AUTO" rampDownDays="14" rampUpDays="14" dormantFactor="0" warnDays="7"/>
    </meadow>
</pastureSeasons>
